Subject: [PATCH] tb710fu start the opt-in native CDC log worker before vfsinit

Base: UniXNU 0c1bac3d51a3009dca1708b15a5198f4b43d057a;
XNU ac9718fb1af618d5ce8678d0dc6e8a58f252216f with the selected complete
arch/pre-OS/macOS/device series through 0011.
Reason: start the independent log transport before source-storage/root setup.
The strong conditional import requires the real selected transport to link;
the worker itself requires tb710fu-cdc=1 and validates live hardware state.
Source: XNU bsd/kern/bsd_init.c and the device-owned CdcXnu.c startup API.
Verification: apply --check on the selected post-0011 source, then actual
arm64e compilation, BSD strong reference and final native symbol checks.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -792,6 +792,10 @@
 	IOKitInitializeTime();
 
 	/* Initialize the file systems. */
+#if defined(XNU_TB710FU_CDC) && XNU_TB710FU_CDC
+	extern void tb710fu_cdc_start(void);
+	tb710fu_cdc_start();
+#endif
 	bsd_init_kprintf("calling vfsinit\n");
 	vfsinit();
 #if defined(XNU_TB710FU_SOURCE_STORAGE) && XNU_TB710FU_SOURCE_STORAGE
